.TH abl-exorcist-assembler 1  "abl-exorcist-assembler 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
abl\-exorcist\-assembler \- Assemble a kernel payload and write the binary image to stdout
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBabl\-exorcist\-assembler\fR [\fB\-\-ramdisk\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIKERNEL\fR> <\fISHIM_OR_INITRD\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Assemble a kernel payload and write the binary image to stdout.
.PP
The default mode appends a compressed kernel package to a raw, device\-appropriate abl\-exorcist AArch64 shim. With \-\-ramdisk, the output is an ABLXRD1 container containing the compressed kernel followed by the supplied initramfs bytes, unchanged. Both modes write the binary image to stdout.
.PP
The kernel is converted to a validated raw arm64 Image before assembly. Device selection, shim provenance, Android boot image geometry, partition writes, and flashing belong to higher\-level consumers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-ramdisk\fR
Build an ABLX ramdisk container instead of a shim+kernel payload
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIKERNEL\fR>
Raw arm64 Image, Image.gz, Image.zst, or Linux EFI zboot image
.TP
<\fISHIM_OR_INITRD\fR>
Raw abl\-exorcist arm64 Image, or initramfs bytes with \-\-ramdisk
.SH VERSION
v0.0.1
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including help and version requests.
.TP
.B 1
An input is invalid or cannot be read, assembly fails, or standard output
cannot be written.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments.
.PP
Diagnostics are written to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Append a kernel package to a shim:
.PP
.EX
abl-exorcist-assembler vmlinuz abl-exorcist.bin > prepared-kernel
.EE
.PP
Build the external-initrd transport used as an Android ramdisk:
.PP
.EX
abl-exorcist-assembler --ramdisk vmlinuz initramfs.img > ablx-ramdisk.img
.EE
